BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:maptimeDavis: Map Room Tour + Open House
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T120000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54038428896368
DESCRIPTION:Learn to search the catalog\, find & handle maps & air photos\
 , use maps & air photos in GIS software\, and use stereoscopes & loupes. S
 ee historic campus maps & air photos! Learn about map collection projects 
 & incoming new materials!\n \n\nSpeaker: Sheena Campbell & Michele Tobias\
 n \n\nUC Davis STEM Librarian\, Sheena Campbell\, provides information lit
 eracy instruction to undergraduate and professional students in the STEM f
 ields\, offers individualized research support\, and identifies resources 
 to enhance the library’s collections. With her background as an artist a
 nd historian\, Sheena’s research interests focus on the intersection of 
 visual culture\, environmental justice\, and the history of scientific tho
 ught.\n \n\nMichele Tobias is a geospatial data scientist with a backgroun
 d in geospatial methods for ecology. Michele earned her PhD from UC Davis 
 in Geography where she studied California’s sandy beach ecosystem with t
 raditional phytosociological methods and innovative remote sensing tools a
 nd was a postdoc at the UC Davis Information Center for the Environment. I
 n her current position as a geospatial data scientist at the UC Davis Libr
 ary\, she applies geospatial tools to new avenues of research across disci
 plines.\n \n\nPrerequisites: None\n \n\nSoftware Required: None
LOCATION:Shields Library Map Room\, 93 Shields Library
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/maptimedavis-map-room-tour-op
 en-house
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shields Library Mural Dedication
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T143000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54066200980920
DESCRIPTION:join us in celebrating our new library mural\, created by unde
 rgraduate students in the Mural Workshop (ART 171/CHI 171) in Spring 2026.
  Drawing on the Chicanx tradition of muralism\, the students' creative pro
 cess centered on community engagement\, collective storytelling\, and sens
 e of place. Vibrant imagery of students\, photos from the library's Univer
 sity Archives\, and an oak tree bearing the words “Saber es Poder” (
 “Knowledge is Power”) are among the elements that explore the library 
 as a space where preservation and empowerment meet. Learn more about the m
 ural.\n\nMeet some of the artists who created the mural and see footage of
  the making of this beautiful work of art. Light refreshments available wh
 ile they last. \nFree and open to all.
LOCATION:Shields Library\, Room 150 (east wing of the first floor)
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/mural-dedication
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
